==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 30~60 seconds<sup>900f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 30~60 seconds<sup>900f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>, delay 30~60 seconds<sup>900f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[One Horn]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Start by sending out a few [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] as you upgrade your [[Worker Cat]], but beware of One Horn. When he appears, stop upgrading the Worker Cat and focus on spawning [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red cats]], such as [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Brave Cat]], [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Brah Cats]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]], along with [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] and some meatshields. Sending out all these units will drain your money reserve, but thanks to B.B.Bunny and Pigge, money shouldn't be much of a problem. When you hit the enemy base, a few more One Horns will spawn, but they too should be of little consequence to your army.

